      "description": {
        "fun": "Basculin is so violent that when a school turns up in a lake, almost everything else disappears, and red- and blue-striped Basculin start fighting the moment they meet. Anglers love the fight it puts up, and many release it into lakes illegally. It was once a common dinner, the fattier red-striped kind being more popular with young people. Its red, white and blue forms may nod to the flag of the United States.",
        "guide": "Basculin is a Water-type fish Pokémon based on a bass, with Red-Striped and Blue-Striped Forms that fight each other on sight. A gentler White-Striped Form lived in ancient Hisui and is the only one that evolves, into Basculegion.",
