      "description": {
        "fun": "Basculegion is a White-Striped Basculin that survived the punishing swim upstream and was joined by the souls of the schoolmates who didn't. Those souls cloak its body and carry it effortlessly up raging rapids, and no fish in Hisui's rivers is its equal. Males are tinged red by the souls' rage and females pale blue by their sadness, perhaps like salmon in spawning colours. It may also draw on the itou, Hokkaidō's 'phantom fish'.",
        "guide": "Basculegion is a Water- and Ghost-type Pokémon that evolves from White-Striped Basculin, cloaked in the souls of Basculin that died swimming upstream. Males are marked red and females pale blue. It was introduced in Pokémon Legends: Arceus.",
